    "q-18350": {
      "dom_id": "step-q18350",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226689/assets/4b0ea03d4978d331f00b3b3aaa30eadc6ebf9eba11eeb5ce24471733dfa5d5ea.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?",
      "worked_solution": "This is the curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ that's been translated \n\n- $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- $2$ units *down*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226689/assets/aec16fd32015f07c13874ddb0ff41da1d5eae62a2b008c4d6aad0e0ab4cb0744.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-(x\\,+\\,1)^{3}\\,-\\,2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
